@novalisek There does exist a shell command that does exactly that, so yes it is possible to do it already, and both bt_gatt_notify and bt_gatt_indicate can have a UUID set to do just what you are proposing: 

https://github.com/zephyrproject-rtos/zephyr/blob/master/include/bluetooth/gatt.h#L828
https://github.com/zephyrproject-rtos/zephyr/blob/master/include/bluetooth/gatt.h#L911

```
static u8_t match_uuid(const struct bt_gatt_attr *attr, void *user_data)
{
	const struct bt_gatt_attr **found = user_data;

	*found = attr;

	return BT_GATT_ITER_STOP;
}

struct bt_gatt_attr *attr;
bt_gatt_foreach_attr_type(handle, 0xffff, uuid, NULL, 1, match_uuid, &attr);
```
@novalisek  You could use `bt_gatt_foreach_attr_type` to find the attribute you are looking for, see example, you can limit the search using the handles to limit it to the service for example.

@Vudentz I think it is a good point made by @novalisek. We should allow attr to be NULL when UUID is passed instead.
